flowchart TD
    A[Ordinary APK or ADB shell] --> B{Reachable entry?}
    B -->|Known public PMS| C[PackageManagerService]
    C --> D{caller + user + protected-package gate}
    D -->|reject| E[No package/HOME mutation]
    D -->|accept only trusted authority| F[State writer]

    A --> G[Amazon private Binder candidate]
    G --> H{ServiceManager / SELinux / permission gate}
    H -->|unknown or denied| E
    H -->|trusted client only| I[Amazon service implementation]
    I --> J{clearCallingIdentity ordering}
    J -->|identity retained| C
    J -->|trusted lifecycle identity| K[KFT/OOBE/other sink]

    A --> L[Native driver candidate]
    L --> M{shipped opener + node policy + domain}
    M -->|not closed| N[Static capability only]
    M -->|trusted native path| O[ION/CMDQ/M4U/uinput/RPMB/etc.]

    A --> P[OTA/recovery candidate]
    P --> Q{signature + AVB + rollback + recovery SELinux}
    Q -->|not proven from app/shell| R[Recovery-only capability]
    Q -->|trusted lifecycle| S[Partition/update sink]

    F --> T[Could change Fire state only with accepted authority]
    K --> T
    O --> U[No demonstrated UID/HOME/package sink]
    S --> V[High-risk; not executed]
